# Security & secrets

## Secrets
- The tracker has **no API keys and no build-time secrets**. Don't add any.
- **Never read, print, echo or commit secrets**: `.env*` (except `.env.example`), `*.pem`, SSH keys, `~/.config/gh/hosts.yml`, `auth.json`, env vars containing KEY/TOKEN/SECRET.
- Never touch `~/.hermes`. Never `git push --force` (or `-f`, `--force-with-lease`, `+refspec`). Never `rm -rf` outside the repo.
- These are enforced by project hooks (`.cursor/hooks/`); if a hook blocks a command, don't work around it — use a safe alternative or ask.

## Privacy
- **No telemetry, analytics, trackers, third-party scripts/fonts/CDNs.** All data stays on the device.
- No runtime network calls. Strict CSP `<meta>` in `index.html`: `default-src 'self'`.
- Render course text as text (no raw `innerHTML` of unescaped content).
